  (global_label "BP265" (shape input) (at 57.336 191.32 90)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid "d2c5c152-4c70-5045-8621-63de4765e03f"))
  (text "Rails, lettered from the factory chart's own E(B+) column: BP310 is the post-choke node — the output-transformer centre tap and both 6V6GT screens sit on it, and this circuit has no screen resistors at all; BP280 is the inverter rail one 10 kΩ dropper below it; BP265 the channel-preamp rail one more below that. Because those droppers also carry channel 2 and the tremolo, netlist.cir drives all three rails at the printed figures rather than deriving a chain missing half its load." (at 12.7 256.098 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left)) (uuid "49d6092c-0be8-539d-bc31-7611d436bb56"))
  (text "Channel 2's 5879 and the 6SQ7 tremolo oscillator are lettered as bottles and left undrawn. Channel 2's screen is fed through the tremolo's Depth network — modulating that screen is how this amplifier makes tremolo — and neither the network nor the channel-2 screen dropper resolves on the only published drawing of this revision. The chart says the same thing loudly: +32 V on that screen against +95 V on channel 1's, off the same +265 V rail. What is legible of both is written out in" (at 12.7 260.498 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left)) (uuid "265130d1-082c-57b6-bcbb-f0e59e3bc3b0"))
  (text "notes.md." (at 12.7 264.898 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left)) (uuid "d25245e3-43e5-5323-b1dd-a104687e06b3"))
  (text "A published restoration records the supply-can complement as 20/10/10/10 µF at 450 WVDC. Three of the four are lettered here; the fourth most likely sits on the +280 V inverter rail, where this reading places no can. The gap is left visible rather than filled." (at 12.7 269.298 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left)) (uuid "75cf467c-43d3-510c-b986-077f92372617"))
  (text "Heaters, the transformer's 5 V and 6.3 V windings, the pilot lamp, the input and speaker jacks and the mains side beyond the transformer (3 A fuse, on/off switch, and the 0.02 µF capacitor the polarity switch grounds onto one line leg or the other) are omitted here — see bom.yaml and layout.yaml. Do not build that mains side as the factory sheet draws it; it predates grounded three-wire practice." (at 12.7 273.698 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left)) (uuid "83de7523-5cb3-5cd7-bc89-d9e5a6e29123"))
  (text "The factory drawing letters no reference designators — not on the bottles, not on the passives — so the designators on this sheet are this corpus's own, functional ones: RL a plate load, RS a screen dropper, CK a cathode bypass, RD a rail dropper." (at 12.7 278.098 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left)) (uuid "246c14b0-9fc3-52a0-b6d4-110c07dfb659"))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
)
